User: In Idaho, 472 people were asked what they call soft drinks. The results of the survey are shown in the pie chart. The central angle of the ``Pop'' sector of the graph is $251^\circ$, to the nearest whole degree. How many of the people surveyed chose ``Pop''? Express your answer as a whole number.

[asy]import graph;
size(150);
real w = 10pt,linew = 1;
filldraw(Arc((0,0),1,0,251)--(0,0)--cycle,gray(.4),black+linewidth(linew));
filldraw(Arc((0,0),1,251,280)--(0,0)--cycle,white,black+linewidth(linew));
filldraw(Arc((0,0),1,280,350)--(0,0)--cycle,gray(.7),black+linewidth(linew));
filldraw(Arc((0,0),1,350,360)--(0,0)--cycle,white,black+linewidth(linew));
label("\textbf{POP}",expi(2.19),expi(2.19),fontsize(w));
